{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Woe to those who plot iniquity</b> — at night, when they are alone with themselves." "<b>to their El</b> — meaning power, not an epithet. And likewise the word טוב and also רע: sometimes it is an epithet of the sacred Name, and sometimes a noun meaning power. And likewise טוב and רע: sometimes it refers to a person who is good or evil, and it is an epithet; and sometimes it refers to an evil thing or a good thing, and it is a noun."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "The phrase 'epithet of the sacred Name' is obscure; possibly referring to divine attributes, but translated literally as the passage may be textually difficult."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:39.300148055Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}